        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 Asian Pacific Society of Respirology.",
        "AbstractText": "We found that simultaneous post-exercise increase in nasal patency and bronchial obstruction occurs only in children with atopic asthma, but not in sensitized children without asthma. In healthy children, the increase in nasal patency is accompanied by bronchial dilatation."
